│ Reasoning:                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│ The issue is that ast.NodeVisitor.visit((1,)) is being represented │
│ as (1) instead of (1,). This is because the repr() function is not │
│ correctly handling the trailing comma in the tuple. We need to     │
│ ensure that repr() preserves the trailing comma when it represents │
│ a single-element tuple. The fix is to simply ensure that the       │
│ repr() function is called with the tuple as is, without any        │
│ modifications.                                                     │
│                                                                    │
